    // cd=11, ab=01: 1
    // cd=11, ab=10: 1
    // cd=11, ab=11: 1

    // From this, the minimal expression is:
    // out = (a & c) | (b & c) | (a & b) | (a & d) | (b & d) | (c & d)

    // But for the case a=0, b=0, c=1, d=0, the correct value is 0, which the original expression gives.
